      "description": "Watch Dundee Utd vs Rangers highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 31, 2026. The spotlight of the Scottish Premiership fell on a high-stakes encounter this July 31, 2026 . Both sides entered the pitch with plenty to prove, setting the stage for a tactical battle where every error would be punished. Rose Provides the First Half Spark After a cagey opening period characterized by midfield duels, the deadlock was finally broken in the 38th minute. Jesse Randall turned provider with a pinpoint pass that found Lachlan Rose in a dangerous position. Rose kept his composure to slot the ball home, giving Dundee United a crucial lead. The goal shifted the momentum, forcing Rangers to rethink their approach as they headed into the halftime break trailing by a single goal. Aasgaard Doubles the Advantage The second half saw Rangers introduce fresh legs, with Youssef Chermiti and Daniel Neil joining the fray. However, their comeback plans were dealt a heavy blow in the 56th minute. Thelo Aasgaard clinical finish doubled the lead for Dundee United , placing them firmly in the driving seat. As the clock ticked down, the match grew increasingly physical, leading to a flurry of yellow cards for players including Vicko Sevelj , Dujon Sterling , and Ross McCrorie . A series of late substitutions followed as both managers looked to manage the closing stages. Despite the pressure from the visitors, Dundee United maintained their shape and discipline. When the final whistle blew after four minutes of stoppage time, it confirmed a professional performance and a vital three points for the home side, leaving Rangers to reflect on missed opportunities."
